    "text": "Leofan men, we secga\u00f0 nu \u00e6rest on \u00feisum gewritum, \u00fe\u00e6t twegen cyningas w\u00e6ron, gecweden on leden\nAn w\u00e6s se Chaldeisca, \u00fee acwealde godes folc on Iudea lande for heora geleafleaste, \u00fea \u00fea hi wur\u00f0odon\n\u00d0a tow\u00e6nde se cyning heora winsuman burh, Hierusalem gehaten, and \u00fe\u00e6t halige templ, \u00f0e Salomon\nHundeseofontig geara hi wunedon \u00fe\u00e6r on \u00feeowte, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t Cyrus cyning hi as\u00e6nde eft ongean to Iudea\nNu w\u00e6s se o\u00fe\u00e6r cyning, \u00fee w\u00e6s gehaten on leden Nabochodonosor, on Syrian lande, \u00fe\u00e6s Cyres sunu,\nHw\u00e6t, \u00fea Cambisus gecw\u00e6\u00f0 to gefeohte ongean Arfaxath, \u00fe\u00e6ra Meda cyning, and he hine ofsloh and\nAc ealle \u00fea leodscipas anmodlice him wi\u00f0cw\u00e6don and as\u00e6ndon his \u00e6rendracan eft sona ongean butan\n\u00d0a gebealh se cyning Nabochodonosor hine sylfne and swor \u00feurh his cynestol, \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde gewrecan\nHe gegaderode his witan \u00f0a and wi\u00f0 hi ealle r\u00e6dde, cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t him swa \u00feuhte, \u00fe\u00e6t he sylf wolde ealne\n\u00dea sende se cyning sumne heretogan, Holofernem gehaten, mid mycelre fyrdinge and bebead him \u00feas\n\u00d0a ferde Holofernis mid orm\u00e6tre fyrde, swa swa se cyning bead, and tobr\u00e6c \u00e6lce burh and \u00fea ofsloh,\nHundtwelftig \u00feusenda wigendra manna w\u00e6ron on his fyrdinge and twelf \u00feusenda scyttena symle him\nAnd nan folc ne mihte his fyrde wi\u00f0standan, ac comon him to of fyrlenum landum, mid fyrhte\nAnd hi swa abugon \u00fea \u00feam breman heretogan mid eallum heora \u00e6htum to \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges anwealde.\nHe ferde \u00fea mid \u00ferymme feohtende swy\u00f0e wi\u00f0 manega leodscipas and heora land gewann, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t\nHi gearcodon swa \u00feeah hi sylfe to wige on \u00feam heagum muntum micclum ymbtrymde and fordytton\nAnd hi anmodlice ealle to gode clypodon, biddende his fultumes, \u00fe\u00e6t hi ne forwurdon.\nHolofernis \u00fea si\u00f0\u00f0an mid his fyrde becom to Iudea lande, \u00fee on god gelyfdon, and his fyrd endemes to\nAc him wear\u00f0 ges\u00e6d, \u00fe\u00e6t hi hi sylfe gegearcodon mid wige him togeanes and woldon him wi\u00f0standan.\nHolofernis \u00fea axode his yldestan cempan, hw\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t mennisc w\u00e6re on \u00f0am muntum wunigende, \u00fee\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 sum heretoga, se hatte Achior, Ammoniscre \u00feeode, mid swi\u00f0licum truwan: Leof, ic \u00fee secge\n\u00deis cynn com iu of Chaldeiscre m\u00e6g\u00f0e and hi \u00e6fre wur\u00feia\u00f0 \u00e6nne \u00e6lmihtigne god, se \u00fee on heofonum\n\u00d0a \u00fea se miccla hunger ealne middaneard ofereode, \u00fea ferdon heora f\u00e6deras \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6r hi fundon him\n\u00d0a wolde Pharao, se Egyptisca cyning, hi yfele geswencan and gesette hi on \u00feeowte to his\nAc hi clypodon endemes to \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan gode, \u00fee hi on gelyfdon, \u00fe\u00e6t he hi ahredde.\nAnd he sona asende syllice witu ofer Egypta lande, o\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6t hi forleton his folc of heora lande faran frige\nHeora god hi \u00fea gel\u00e6dde of \u00feam lande ealle ofer \u00fea readan s\u00e6, si\u00f0igende be \u00feam grunde, swa \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t\nAnd Pharao, se cyning, ferde him \u00e6thindan, wolde hi habban eft to his \u00feeowte.\nAc god hine adr\u00e6ncte on \u00fe\u00e6re deopan s\u00e6, \u00fe\u00e6t of ealre his fyrde an mann ne belaf.\n\u00d0\u00e6t godes folc \u00fea eode upp be \u00feam grunde, herigende heora drihten, \u00fee hi swa ahredde, and hi\nAnd him d\u00e6ghwamlice com \u00feurh heora drihtnes sande mete of heofenum eallum \u00feam mancynne and\nHi gewunnon sy\u00f0\u00f0an mid sige \u00f0ysne eard, and heora god him fylste and feaht for hi, and ne mihte nan\nSwa oft swa hi bugon fram his biggengum to \u00feam h\u00e6\u00f0enum godum, hi wurdon gehergode and to\nSwa oft swa hi gecyrdon mid so\u00f0re d\u00e6dbote eft to heora gode, he gedyde hi sona mihtige and strange\nHeora god so\u00felice hata\u00f0 unrihtwisnysse.\nNu for manegum gearum, \u00fea \u00fea hi misheoldon \u00feone heofonlican god, hi wurdon gehergode and sume\nIc bidde \u00fee nu, hlaford, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu l\u00e6te ofaxian, gif \u00f0is folc nu h\u00e6bbe \u00e6nige unrihtwisnysse o\u00f0\u00f0e gylt\nGif hi \u00feonne nabba\u00f0 nane unrihtwisnysse, ne heora gode abolgen, \u00feonne beo we ealle to hospe gedone\nHolofernis \u00fea sona \u00e6fter \u00feissere segene gebealh hine swi\u00f0e and mid gebeote cw\u00e6\u00f0: Wite \u00f0u nu,\nHe het hine \u00fea gebindan and gebringan on \u00fe\u00e6t land and \u00feam folce bet\u00e6can, \u00fe\u00e6t he mid him forwurde.\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea gebunden, swa swa se brema het, and to \u00f0am lande gel\u00e6d and forleton hine \u00fe\u00e6r to anum\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea afunden fram \u00f0am folce \u00fe\u00e6r and he him eall s\u00e6de his si\u00f0 be \u00e6ndebyrdnysse.\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6t folc \u00fea sona \u00e6fter his segene feollon to eor\u00f0an mid flowendum tearum, cwe\u00f0ende mid\nHi \u00fea gefrefrodon \u00feone fores\u00e6dan Achior and Ozias heora heafodmann hine h\u00e6fde mid him.\nAnd hi b\u00e6don \u00fea ealle godes mildheortnysse and his gescyldnysse wi\u00f0 \u00feone Syriscan here.\nHw\u00e6t, \u00fea Holofernus wolde hi ut asittan and he heora w\u00e6terscipe mid weardmannum besette twentig\n\u00d0\u00e6t Israhela folc \u00fea wear\u00f0 geangsumod on mode for \u00fe\u00e6re w\u00e6terleaste.\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6r witodlice n\u00e6s on eallum \u00feam \u00feyttum, \u00fee on \u00fe\u00e6re byrig w\u00e6ron, swa mycel w\u00e6teres d\u00e6l, \u00fe\u00e6t\nAc hi leton \u00fea to r\u00e6de, \u00fe\u00e6t hi woldon abugan \u00feam breman heretogan to his mannr\u00e6dene, \u00fe\u00e6t hi\nOzias \u00f0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 to eallum \u00feam folce: Mine gebro\u00f0ru, beo\u00f0 eow ge\u00f0yldige and mid emnum mode\n\u00d0a w\u00e6s on \u00fe\u00e6re byrig on \u00feam ylcan timan an \u00e6nlic wimman on wudewanhade, Iudith gehaten, \u00fe\u00e6ra\nSwi\u00f0e gelyfed mann on \u00feone lyfigendan god, hlisfull on \u00feeawum, rihtlice lybbende \u00e6fter Moyses \u00e6,\nHe l\u00e6fde \u00fe\u00e6re wudewan unlytel on feo and on o\u00f0rum \u00e6htum, \u00e6fter his gebyrdum mycele welan on\nAnd hi wunode on cl\u00e6nnysse \u00e6fter hire were on hyre upflore mid hire \u00feinenum.\nHeo w\u00e6s swi\u00f0e wlitig and wenlices hiwes and heo f\u00e6ste symle buton on freolsdagum, mid h\u00e6ran\n\u00d0eos Iudith ofaxode, hu Ozias gespr\u00e6c, and cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t hit w\u00e6re witodlice unr\u00e6d, \u00fe\u00e6t mann sceolde\nNe gladia\u00f0 \u00feas word god us to miltsunge, ac hi hine gremia\u00f0 to gramlicre yrsunge.\nWe sceolon beon gemyndige his mildheortnysse, for\u00fean \u00f0e we nyton n\u00e6nne o\u00f0erne god buton hine\nUton andbidian mid eadmodnysse his anes frofres.\nAbraham and Isaac and ure heahf\u00e6deras wurdon afandode.\nOn heora frecednyssum and on earfo\u00f0nyssum hi w\u00e6ron getrywe \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan gode, \u00fee hi \u00e6fre\nHine we sceolon biddan, \u00fe\u00e6t he us geblissige and of \u00feyssere earfo\u00f0nysse us generige.\n\u00c6fter \u00feisum wordum and o\u00f0rum gebedum heo awearp hire h\u00e6ran and hire wudewan reaf and hi sylfe\nAnd eode hire sy\u00f0\u00f0an mid anre \u00feinene ut of \u00fe\u00e6re byrig and bebead \u00feam folce and \u00feam fores\u00e6dan\nAnd hi ealle wundrodon hire wlites swi\u00f0e.\nHeo \u00f0a on \u00e6rnemergen to \u00feam weardum becom, s\u00e6de, \u00fe\u00e6t heo wolde gesecan \u00feone ealdormann and\nHi \u00f0a wundrodon hire wlites swi\u00f0e and hire wislicra worda and mid wur\u00f0mynte hi gel\u00e6ddon to heora\nSona swa he beseah on hire scinendan nebbwlite, swa wear\u00f0 he gegripen mid \u00f0\u00e6re galnysse his\nAnd heo aleat to his fotum, s\u00e6de, \u00fe\u00e6t heo wiste to gewissan \u00feinge, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t Israhela folc swa yfle w\u00e6s\nHeo cw\u00e6\u00f0 eft o\u00f0rum worde: Ic wur\u00f0ige minne god eac swilce mid \u00fee and on asettum timan ic sceal\nFor \u00fei ic com to \u00fee, \u00fe\u00e6t ic cydde \u00fee \u00feis.\nHe gelyfde \u00fea hire wordum and hire wel behet.\nAnd his \u00feegenas s\u00e6don, \u00fe\u00e6t swylc wimman n\u00e6re on ealre eor\u00f0an swa f\u00e6geres wlites and swa wis on\nAnd se ealdorman hi het gan into his madmum and \u00fe\u00e6r wunian, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he hyre word sende.\nAnd he het his hiredmen hire \u00feenian of his agenum \u00feenungum and his estmetum.\nAc heo nolde swa \u00feeah his sanda brucan for his h\u00e6\u00f0enscipe, ac heo h\u00e6fde gebroht on hire \u00feinene\nIudith \u00fea ab\u00e6d \u00e6t \u00feam ealdormen, \u00fe\u00e6t heo moste be leafe on \u00f0am langum nihtum gan on hyre\nAnd he sealde hire leafe, \u00fe\u00e6t heo swa don moste.\nAnd heo swa dyde symle on nihtum, b\u00e6d \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan god, \u00fe\u00e6t he hire gewissode his folce to\n\u00d0a on \u00feam feor\u00f0an d\u00e6ge feormode se ealdorman his heah\u00feegnas on his getelde on micelre blisse and\nHeo com \u00fea geglenged for nanre galnysse and stod him \u00e6tforan swi\u00f0e f\u00e6gres hiwes, and his mod sona\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 Holofernis wundorlice bli\u00f0e ealne \u00feone d\u00e6g and fordr\u00e6ncte hine sylfne mid \u00feam strangum\nAnd ealle his \u00feegnas eac w\u00e6ron fordr\u00e6ncte and hi efston on \u00e6fnunge to heora mane swi\u00f0e.\nAnd \u00fea bur\u00feegnas gebrohton \u00feone ealdormann on anum bedde mid \u00fe\u00e6re Iudith and na swi\u00f0e ne\nIudith geseah \u00fea, \u00fea \u00fea he on sl\u00e6pe w\u00e6s, \u00fe\u00e6t hire w\u00e6s gerymed to hire r\u00e6de wel for\u00f0, and het hire\nHeo nam \u00f0a \u00fe\u00e6t heafod and his hopscytan and eode hire ut mid hire \u00feinene swylce on gebedum, swa\nIudith \u00fea clypode and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00feam weardmannum: Undo\u00f0 \u00feas burhgatu.\nGod sylf is mid us, se \u00fee mihte gefremode on Israhela \u00feeode.\nAnd hi \u00fea ardlice undydon \u00fea gatu and comon endemes mid leohte hire to, for\u00fean \u00fee hi wendon, \u00fe\u00e6t\nHeo astah \u00fea up to anum steapum beorge and \u00e6tywde \u00fe\u00e6t heafod him eallum, cwe\u00f0ende: Heria\u00f0, ic\nAnd he ofsloh nu to niht on minum handum his folces feond.\nAnd heo unforht cw\u00e6\u00f0: Godes engel so\u00f0lice me gescylde wi\u00f0 hine, \u00fe\u00e6t ic unwemme eft becom to\nHi sceawodon \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6t heafod mid swi\u00f0licre wafunge and Ozias, heora ealdor, and hi ealle samod\n\u00d0a com Achior, Holofernes \u00feegen, se \u00f0e \u00e6r him gecydde godes gecy\u00f0nysse, and him swa aeode, swa\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea afyrht \u00e6t fruman swi\u00f0e for \u00f0\u00e6re gesih\u00fee, \u00fea \u00fea he sceawode \u00fe\u00e6t heafod.\nAc he blissode sona and bletsode Iudith and gelyfde si\u00f0\u00f0an on \u00feone lyfigendan god \u00e6fter Moyses \u00e6,\nIudith \u00fea bebead \u00feam burhwarum \u00feus: Asetta\u00f0 \u00feis heafod on \u00feam hehstan wealle and ga\u00f0 eow\n\u00deonne beo\u00f0 eowre fynd afyrhte for eow, \u00feonne hi heafodleasne heora ealdorman finda\u00f0.\n\u00deonne mage ge gewyrcan eower word on him.\nHi dydon \u00fea swa sona on d\u00e6gred and gew\u00e6pnode utferdon mid folclicum truman, swi\u00f0e hlydende to\nAc nan man ne dorste \u00fea duru unlucan, ac hi woldon elles mid gehlyde hine awreccan.\n\u00d0a \u00fea him \u00fe\u00e6s ne speow \u00feurh heora hludan spr\u00e6ce, \u00fea as\u00e6ndon hi inn \u00e6nne his bur\u00f0ena.\nAnd se afunde his hlaford licgan heafodleasne and he \u00fea mid wanunge wende ut ongean, secende\nHer li\u00f0 se ealdormann heafodleas on bedde, mid his blode besyled.\nHi wurdon \u00fea afyrhte wundorlice ealle and butan \u00e6lcum r\u00e6de bysmorlice flugon to heora lande weard\nAnd of eallum heora burgum Ozias asende him maran fultum and afligdon hi endemes of heora earde,\nIsrahela folc \u00fea mid \u00e6nlicum sige wendon him hamweard and \u00fea herelafa d\u00e6ldon betwux him on\nAnd hi ealle bet\u00e6hton Holofernes \u00feing Iudithe to h\u00e6bbenne.\nAnd hi heredon \u00fea god mid swi\u00felicre blisse on sange and on dreame.\nIoachim w\u00e6s gehaten heora yldesta sacerd.\nSe com of Hierusalem mid eallum his preostum to Bethulian byrig mid mycelre blisse, \u00fe\u00e6t he Iudith\nAnd hi hi swi\u00f0e bletsodon, ealle \u00feisum wordum: \u00feu eart wuldor so\u00f0lice ure byrig Hierusalem and\nIudith \u00fea herode \u00feone heofonlican god swy\u00f0e mid lofsange, swa swa hit on l\u00e6den us s\u00e6g\u00f0.\nAnd hi ealle offrodon heora lac gode binnan Hierusalem bli\u00f0e for \u00f0am sige.\nIudith \u00fea \u00feurhwunode on hire wudewanhade m\u00e6rlice for gode on micclum wur\u00f0mynte.\nHundteontig geara heo leofode and hire lytlan heo freode.\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6t Israhela folc eall wunode on sibbe on eallum hire life and eac lange sy\u00f0\u00f0an.\nNis \u00feis nan leas spel: hit stent on leden, nis on \u00f0\u00e6re bibliothecan.\n\u00de\u00e6t witon boceras, \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t leden cunnon, \u00fe\u00e6t we na ne leoga\u00f0.\nOn hire w\u00e6s gefylled \u00fe\u00e6s h\u00e6lendes cwyde: \u00e6lc, \u00fee hine ahef\u00f0, sceal beon geeadmet and se \u00fee hine\nHeo eadmod and cl\u00e6ne and ofercom \u00feone modigan, lytel and unstrang and alede \u00feone micclan, for\u00f0an\nIudith behet \u00e6rest \u00feam welhreowum ealdormen, \u00fe\u00e6t heo wolde hine gebringan binnan to hire folce.\nAc hit n\u00e6s na ealles leas, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t heo him behet, \u00fea \u00fea heo b\u00e6r his heafod binnan \u00feam weallum and\n\u00deam sy a wur\u00f0mynt to worulde.\nAmen.\nHeo nolde agan, swa swa us s\u00e6g\u00f0 seo racu, \u00fe\u00e6s w\u00e6lhreowan h\u00e6rereaf, \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t folc hire forgeaf, ac\nSume nunnan syndon, \u00fee sceandlice libba\u00f0, tella\u00f0 to lytlum gylte, \u00fe\u00e6t hi hi forlicgon and \u00fe\u00e6t hi\nAc heo ne bi\u00f0 na eft m\u00e6den, gif heo hi \u00e6ne forlig\u00f0, ne heo n\u00e6f\u00f0 \u00fea mede \u00fe\u00e6s hundfealdan w\u00e6stmes.\nNima\u00f0 eow bysne be \u00feyssere Iudith, hu cl\u00e6nlice heo leofode \u00e6r Cristes acennednysse, and ne leoga\u00f0\nIc wylle eac secgan, min swustor, \u00fe\u00e6t m\u00e6g\u00f0had and cl\u00e6nnys mycele mihte habba\u00f0, swa swa we\nMalchus \u00f0a eode ut of \u00f0am scr\u00e6fe mid his gemacan mycclum ablicged.\nAnd hi namon \u00fea hors, \u00f0e hi \u00feyder brohton, and w\u00e6ron \u00f0a ridende, \u00f0e \u00e6r w\u00e6ron fe\u00f0ende, and\n\u00d0am sy wuldor and lof a to worulde.\nAmen.",
